watch?v=ckqO3n-4IOI","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/are-ai-coding-skills-just-hype-i-tested-them-p1tp8ypz6","summary":null,"image":"https://i.ytimg.com/vi/ckqO3n-4IOI/sddefault.jpg","num_upvotes":1,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2026-05-02T17:03:52.000Z"},{"id":"6MHeV0eNw","title":"GPT Image 2 is amazing for stock photos","url":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=dJa2EvFDTkk","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/gpt-image-2-is-amazing-for-stock-photos-6mhev0enw","summary":null,"image":"https://i.ytimg.com/vi/dJa2EvFDTkk/sddefault.jpg","num_upvotes":0,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2026-05-01T16:02:42.000Z"},{"id":"oUaq25oAj","title":"This Claude Skill Saves Me Hours on Every Landing Page","url":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=tfVAMTMUPk8","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/this-claude-skill-saves-me-hours-on-every-landing-page-ouaq25oaj","summary":null,"image":"https://i.ytimg.com/vi/tfVAMTMUPk8/sddefault.jpg","num_upvotes":0,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2026-05-01T13:36:56.000Z"},{"id":"x89h4TgDz","title":"I Didn\u2019t Expect This: Opus 4.7 vs GPT 5.5","url":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=p2-z1v6Zjuk","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/i-didn-t-expect-this-opus-4-7-vs-gpt-5-5-x89h4tgdz","summary":null,"image":"https://i.ytimg.com/vi/p2-z1v6Zjuk/sddefault.jpg","num_upvotes":1,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2026-04-30T16:13:12.000Z"},{"id":"nRXaPZq2v","title":"AI plugin that automates git commits and pull request descriptions","url":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=TpoJ044l0Q8","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/this-one-skill-eliminates-pr-busywork-nrxapzq2v","summary":"A developer showcases a custom AI-powered plugin called 'Agentic System Labs Essentials' that automates the pull request workflow. The tool analyzes staged changes, groups them into logical commits, proposes a branch name, generates a descriptive PR description, links relevant GitHub issues, suggests reviewers, and auto-tags labels. The demo walks through installing the plugin, running the 'ship PR' skill, reviewing the AI-generated commit plan, and confirming the final pull request on GitHub. The plugin requires the GitHub CLI to be authenticated and is open source.","image":"https://i.ytimg.com/vi/TpoJ044l0Q8/sddefault.jpg","num_upvotes":0,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2026-04-28T13:44:52.000Z"},{"id":"V2OGA1qjF","title":"Practical uses of GPT Image 2 for web projects and side projects","url":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=5JJohLtp1Ug","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/i-didn-t-expect-gpt-image-2-to-be-this-good-v2oga1qjf","summary":"A hands-on walkthrough of OpenAI's GPT Image 2 model, showcasing practical use cases including generating open graph images from website URLs, extracting and fixing perspective on phone screenshots, creating transparent cutouts, and redesigning landing page hero sections. The author demonstrates integrating Image 2 into side projects like an icon generator and an AI clip studio, highlighting the model's text rendering quality and image editing capabilities.","image":"https://i.ytimg.com/vi/5JJohLtp1Ug/sddefault.jpg","num_upvotes":0,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2026-04-26T13:49:29.000Z"},{"id":"IOOfsc26D","title":"Understanding Opus 4.7 Effort Level","url":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=xBfEeBAHLt4","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/understanding-opus-4-7-effort-level-ioofsc26d","summary":"A walkthrough of how effort levels work in Claude's Opus 4.7 model, based on a Reddit post. Key points: effort is a behavioral signal controlling adaptive reasoning depth, tool call appetite, response length, and agentic autonomy \u2014 not a strict token budget. Opus 4.7 defaults to 'extra high' effort on all plans including Pro, while Opus 4.6 defaulted to 'medium' on Pro/Max plans, explaining why some users perceived a quality drop. Low effort Opus 4.7 roughly equals medium effort Opus 4.6. Importantly, context quality can matter more than effort level \u2014 a well-contextualized low-effort prompt often beats a poorly-contextualized max-effort one. Opus 4.7 also uses 10\u201335% more tokens than 4.6, so matching effort level to task complexity (e.g., Sonnet low for simple tasks, Opus max for architecture/security) is important for managing token costs.","image":"https://i.ytimg.com/vi/xBfEeBAHLt4/sddefault.jpg","num_upvotes":0,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2026-04-24T12:48:19.000Z"},{"id":"ZcHkRVd6y","title":"Can Opus 4.7 Refactor NextJs to Tanstack Start?","url":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=JYEZOhNdpjg","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/can-opus-4-7-refactor-nextjs-to-tanstack-start--zchkrvd6y","summary":"An experiment using Claude Code's max effort level to refactor a production Next.js app (with tRPC) to TanStack Start. The author walks through the full process: setting up the prompt, running a 28-minute planning session that consumed ~33% of a 5-hour session budget, iteratively fixing errors (config issues, React SSR incompatibilities, auth migration from NextAuth to Auth.js v5, S3 bucket port mismatches), and ultimately getting the app running locally with 103 file changes. Key takeaways include keeping refactoring scope narrow, running security audits on auth/middleware changes post-refactor, and setting up a staging environment before merging to production.","image":"https://i.ytimg.com/vi/JYEZOhNdpjg/sddefault.jpg","num_upvotes":32,"num_comments":6,"created_at":"2026-04-23T12:53:28.000Z"},{"id":"915C2Lrv7","title":"Claude Design Is Breaking My Workflow (In a Good Way)","url":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=i90wX-lP0g4","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/claude-design-is-breaking-my-workflow-in-a-good-way--915c2lrv7","summary":"A hands-on walkthrough of Claude Design (Anthropic's new AI design tool), exploring its ability to generate wireframes and high-fidelity UI prototypes from text prompts. The author tests it on three projects: a course platform dashboard, an AI agent system dashboard, and a zombie survival game HUD. Claude Design asks clarifying questions, generates multiple design variations, and produces downloadable HTML/CSS files that can be fed into Claude Code via Cursor to apply the designs to an existing codebase. The author is impressed by how quickly it transforms rough prototypes into polished-looking UIs.","image":"https://i.ytimg.com/vi/i90wX-lP0g4/sddefault.jpg","num_upvotes":0,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2026-04-21T17:41:15.000Z"}],"similar_handles":["dotnet","coredumpped","bytegrad","mentaloutlaw","vuemastery"],"opposite_handles":["horde","watercooler","dailydevworld","alexfinn","tbpn"],"similar":[{"id":"dotnet","handle":"dotnet","name":".NET Blog","is_squad":false,"x":-7.2879,"y":-9.7322,"cluster_id":3,"posts_collected":462,"image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/t_logo,f_auto/v1/logos/f23eb59371bd4f07aeef64c4eef73266","features_preview":{"posts_per_week":2.726935,"median_upvotes":1.0,"author_present_share":0.0,"hype_score":0.031385,"avg_read_time":21.835498,"tag_diversity":0.324675},"top_tags_preview":[[".net",389],["c#",91],["ai",91]],"view_coords":{"engagement_style":[3.2647,-0.0147],"cadence_depth":[8.2353,8.8824],"hype_variety":[6.8824,5.1029],"title_style":[6.2647,-1.9706]}},{"id":"coredumpped","handle":"coredumpped","name":"Core Dumped","is_squad":false,"x":-7.1665,"y":-9.6029,"cluster_id":3,"posts_collected":43,"image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/s--N9ie6ehW--/f_auto/v1725038034/logos/coredumpped","features_preview":{"posts_per_week":0.514627,"median_upvotes":1.0,"author_present_share":0.0,"hype_score":0.0,"avg_read_time":16.325581,"tag_diversity":0.604651},"top_tags_preview":[["computer-science",11],["rust",7],["c",7]],"view_coords":{"engagement_style":[3.3382,-1.9265],"cadence_depth":[-5.0735,8.2647],"hype_variety":[-6.9706,-3.1176],"title_style":[9.0588,-1.9853]}},{"id":"bytegrad","handle":"bytegrad","name":"ByteGrad","is_squad":false,"x":-6.932,"y":-